WEBVTT

00:00:04.863 --> 00:00:07.634
Billy Elliot by Melvin Burgess.

00:00:07.694 --> 00:00:11.746
Based on a motion picture screenplay written by Lee Hall.

00:00:11.806 --> 00:00:17.558
Copyright 2005, Universal Studios Licensing, LLLP.

00:00:17.618 --> 00:00:25.761
Adapted by Jackie bluesy.

00:00:25.821 --> 00:00:29.272
I love to boogie.

00:00:29.332 --> 00:00:32.188
I hate my brother.

00:00:32.248 --> 00:00:36.826
He's stupid, but he has got some good music.

00:00:36.886 --> 00:00:40.890
I listen to his music when he's out at work with my dad.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:45.374
Well, they're not at work, not now.

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:47.616
They're on strike.

00:00:47.676 --> 00:00:51.420
But they still go to the mine every day.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.502
Nan loves the music too.

00:00:54.562 --> 00:00:57.316
Tony and Dad leave in the morning.

00:00:57.376 --> 00:00:59.980
Then the music goes on.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.364
I make breakfast for us and we both dance.

00:01:03.424 --> 00:01:05.915
I can hear her in her bedroom.

00:01:05.975 --> 00:01:09.506
She tries to dance, but she can't walk very well now.

00:01:09.566 --> 00:01:12.308
Well, she is 80.

00:01:12.368 --> 00:01:17.080
This morning, I made the eggs and danced to her bedroom.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.271
Hey, Nan, breakfast, I called.

00:01:20.331 --> 00:01:22.962
I opened the door with my foot and...

00:01:23.022 --> 00:01:26.474
Oh, no, not again.

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.852
Her bed was empty.

00:01:28.911 --> 00:01:33.392
I put the eggs on the kitchen table and ran out of the house.

00:01:33.452 --> 00:01:35.384
Where was she?

00:01:35.444 --> 00:01:37.376
She does this a lot.

00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:39.389
She forgets things.

00:01:39.448 --> 00:01:41.931
She forgets her name.

00:01:41.991 --> 00:01:44.334
I looked up the street.

00:01:44.394 --> 00:01:45.594
Nan?

00:01:45.654 --> 00:01:46.886
Nan?

00:01:46.946 --> 00:01:48.638
Which way?

00:01:48.697 --> 00:01:50.593
Then I had an idea.

00:01:50.653 --> 00:01:53.950
I ran to the end of the street and up to some trees.

00:01:54.009 --> 00:01:55.860
There she was.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.133
She often goes there.

00:01:58.192 --> 00:01:59.674
Why?

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.356
Who knows?

00:02:01.416 --> 00:02:04.518
Maybe she played there when she was little.

00:02:04.578 --> 00:02:07.150
She looked frightened.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.092
Who are you?

00:02:09.152 --> 00:02:10.653
She said.

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:14.050
It's me, Nan, Billy.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.517
She didn't look very happy.

00:02:16.577 --> 00:02:18.558
Then we both heard something.

00:02:18.618 --> 00:02:20.070
Behind us.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.971
On the road.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.103
We saw them.

00:02:24.162 --> 00:02:26.134
Lots of them.

00:02:26.194 --> 00:02:28.276
The police.

00:02:28.336 --> 00:02:32.118
Their clothes were black and they had battens.

00:02:32.177 --> 00:02:34.640
Nan looked at me.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.641
What are they?

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.232
She asked.

00:02:38.292 --> 00:02:40.104
Police Nan.

00:02:40.164 --> 00:02:41.964
It's the police.

00:02:42.024 --> 00:02:44.262
Are they here for us?

00:02:44.322 --> 00:02:45.739
She asked.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.260
No nan.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.543
Not us, I said.

00:02:49.603 --> 00:02:51.896
Is it Jackie?

00:02:51.956 --> 00:02:53.257
Is it Tony?

00:02:53.317 --> 00:02:54.268
She asked.

00:02:54.328 --> 00:02:55.940
I didn't answer.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.422
I didn't want to know the answer.

00:02:58.482 --> 00:03:03.491
I took my nan's arm and we walked slowly home.

00:03:03.551 --> 00:03:06.186
I loved to boogie.

00:03:06.246 --> 00:03:07.998
Jitterbug boogie.

00:03:08.058 --> 00:03:12.082
I'm trying to play cosmic boogie on the piano and thinking about ma'am.

00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:13.874
It was her piano.

00:03:13.933 --> 00:03:15.604
Ma'am's dead.

00:03:15.664 --> 00:03:17.918
She died two years ago.

00:03:17.978 --> 00:03:20.109
I think about her a lot.

00:03:20.169 --> 00:03:22.120
I've got a letter from her.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.483
She wrote it before she died.

00:03:24.543 --> 00:03:27.826
I'm still here, Billy, she wrote.

00:03:27.886 --> 00:03:29.888
But she isn't here.

00:03:29.948 --> 00:03:31.941
She's dead.

00:03:32.001 --> 00:03:34.395
Man was good at the piano.

00:03:34.454 --> 00:03:36.206
She played for all of us.

00:03:36.266 --> 00:03:39.258
I'd like piano lessons, but they're too expensive.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:41.150
We haven't got the money.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.692
My dad's always telling us that.

00:03:43.752 --> 00:03:45.784
We haven't got much.

00:03:45.844 --> 00:03:48.746
Not now that there's a strike.

00:03:48.806 --> 00:03:51.939
Billy, stop that.

00:03:51.999 --> 00:03:53.871
It's Dad.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.802
He's going out again with Tony in a minute.

00:03:56.862 --> 00:03:58.814
Why do I have to stop?

00:03:58.874 --> 00:04:00.906
He's not going to be here.

00:04:00.966 --> 00:04:01.961
Why?

00:04:02.021 --> 00:04:03.626
Then I say the wrong thing.

00:04:03.686 --> 00:04:08.019
If it was ma'am, Dad comes over.

00:04:08.079 --> 00:04:10.821
He closes the piano with a bang.

00:04:10.881 --> 00:04:13.873
I'm not telling you again.

00:04:13.933 --> 00:04:16.334
I go to my room.

00:04:16.394 --> 00:04:23.090
Back to Tony's music.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:30.837
Chapter 2 Billy.

00:04:30.897 --> 00:04:33.761
Boys don't do ballet.

00:04:33.821 --> 00:04:39.038
Billy Elliot, this isn't a tea party, it's a boxing lesson.

00:04:39.098 --> 00:04:40.584
Heat him!

00:04:40.643 --> 00:04:45.068
It's Saturday morning and I'm at the boxing club at the social.

00:04:45.128 --> 00:04:49.370
This morning I'm against Greavesy and he's bigger than me.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.132
I have my own ideas about boxing.

00:04:52.192 --> 00:04:54.172
It's all about your feet.

00:04:54.232 --> 00:04:56.724
So I run and turn and jump.

00:04:56.784 --> 00:04:58.484
I move quickly.

00:04:58.544 --> 00:05:01.246
Greavesy just stands there.

00:05:01.306 --> 00:05:04.168
George, the teacher, isn't happy.

00:05:04.228 --> 00:05:05.540
Hit him.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.470
Don't dance around.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.511
Bang.

00:05:08.571 --> 00:05:10.032
I'm on the floor.

00:05:10.092 --> 00:05:13.234
Greaves is standing over me and is smiling.

00:05:13.294 --> 00:05:15.075
I can hear George.

00:05:15.135 --> 00:05:17.066
Billy Elliot, get up.

00:05:17.126 --> 00:05:19.148
You're going to do it right.

00:05:19.208 --> 00:05:21.648
You're not going home yet.

00:05:21.708 --> 00:05:23.370
I get up.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:25.972
George pulls me to the punch bag.

00:05:26.032 --> 00:05:27.472
Hit it.

00:05:27.532 --> 00:05:33.676
Your poor father, he pays for boxing lessons, and this happens.

00:05:33.736 --> 00:05:38.278
And on, and on, and on.

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.641
I'm angry now.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.932
I hit the punch bag.

00:05:42.992 --> 00:05:46.024
I hate the punch bag.

00:05:46.084 --> 00:05:51.138
Arms up, and one, and two, and three, and four.

00:05:51.198 --> 00:05:53.280
Feel the music.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:57.641
On the other side of the room, there's a ballet class.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.451
Someone's playing the piano.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:04.074
One and two and three and four.

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:08.308
As the music plays, I hit the punch bag.

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:11.430
One and two and bang and hit.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:14.713
And three and four and hit and bang.

00:06:14.772 --> 00:06:17.564
That's better, George says.

00:06:17.624 --> 00:06:20.228
Stay here and get it right.

00:06:20.287 --> 00:06:22.178
See you next week.

00:06:22.238 --> 00:06:24.060
And he goes out.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.867
All the other boys go too.

00:06:26.926 --> 00:06:30.542
Right girls and one and two.

00:06:30.602 --> 00:06:32.212
Debbie, don't look at me.

00:06:32.272 --> 00:06:33.663
Look in front of you.

00:06:33.723 --> 00:06:35.984
And three and four.

00:06:36.044 --> 00:06:37.814
I go and watch.

00:06:37.874 --> 00:06:39.455
It's clever.

00:06:39.514 --> 00:06:41.736
They all dance together.

00:06:41.795 --> 00:06:45.556
Left and two and down and two and turn and two.

00:06:45.616 --> 00:06:46.927
I try it.

00:06:46.987 --> 00:06:48.488
I stretch out my leg.

00:06:48.548 --> 00:06:50.765
Yeah, easy.

00:06:50.825 --> 00:06:52.994
Why don't you try?

00:06:53.054 --> 00:06:54.364
It's Debbie.

00:06:54.424 --> 00:06:56.146
She goes to my school.

00:06:56.206 --> 00:06:57.947
Nah, I say.

00:06:58.007 --> 00:06:59.948
Boys don't do ballet.

00:07:00.008 --> 00:07:01.701
Legs up.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.242
They all stretch their legs.

00:07:04.302 --> 00:07:10.458
Mrs Wilkinson, she's a teacher, walks around and looks closely at each leg.

00:07:10.518 --> 00:07:12.388
I try it.

00:07:12.448 --> 00:07:14.440
Debbie laughs at me.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.562
Your legs moving.

00:07:16.622 --> 00:07:18.063
I look down.

00:07:18.123 --> 00:07:19.560
She's right.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.108
I'm wearing boxing shoes, I tell her.

00:07:23.168 --> 00:07:26.710
Mrs Wilkinson takes a cigarette from a pocket.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.580
She smokes a lot.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:34.144
Okay girls, and one and two and three and four.

00:07:34.203 --> 00:07:36.285
I want to do it too.

00:07:36.345 --> 00:07:38.646
I try, but it's difficult.

00:07:38.706 --> 00:07:40.928
I start to listen to the music.

00:07:40.988 --> 00:07:42.688
It's easier then.

00:07:42.748 --> 00:07:46.008
Shoes off, Mrs in front of me.

00:07:46.068 --> 00:07:50.859
Not me miss, I start to say, but she's already walking down the room.

00:07:50.919 --> 00:07:55.681
I take off my shoes and then she's back again, with ballet shoes.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.882
Here you are, she says.

00:07:57.941 --> 00:08:00.653
You can't dance in boxing shoes.

00:08:00.712 --> 00:08:05.684
I don't know, but then I think, why not?

00:08:05.744 --> 00:08:08.276
So I do it.

00:08:08.335 --> 00:08:10.867
I do ballet for the first time.

00:08:10.926 --> 00:08:14.260
It isn't easy, but miss is a good teacher.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:18.123
We're all standing on one leg with the other leg behind.

00:08:18.183 --> 00:08:20.203
Miss comes over.

00:08:20.263 --> 00:08:24.104
I like the leg, she says, and then walks off.

00:08:24.164 --> 00:08:27.414
She doesn't say much, but I'm happy.

00:08:27.474 --> 00:08:30.785
I'm walking home later and Miss drives by.

00:08:30.845 --> 00:08:33.355
She sees me and stops the car.

00:08:33.415 --> 00:08:35.826
Debbie's sitting in the back.

00:08:35.886 --> 00:08:37.376
Oh, I think.

00:08:37.436 --> 00:08:39.256
Debbie's her daughter.

00:08:39.316 --> 00:08:41.547
Miss is still smoking.

00:08:41.607 --> 00:08:43.310
She looks at me.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.964
It's 50p a lesson, you know.

00:08:46.024 --> 00:08:48.336
Bring me the money next week.

00:08:48.396 --> 00:08:49.708
I can't.

00:08:49.768 --> 00:08:51.148
I'm going to boxing.

00:08:51.209 --> 00:08:54.542
You're terrible at boxing, says Debbie and laughs.

00:08:54.602 --> 00:08:56.242
Be quiet.

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:59.626
Miss looks round at Debbie and then back at me.

00:08:59.686 --> 00:09:01.537
Didn't you enjoy it today?

00:09:01.557 --> 00:09:04.058
I don't say anything.

00:09:04.118 --> 00:09:07.662
It's your life, she says, and off they go.

00:09:07.722 --> 00:09:09.752
Miss was right.

00:09:09.812 --> 00:09:11.634
I enjoyed it.

00:09:11.694 --> 00:09:14.254
But the music was a bit boring.

00:09:14.314 --> 00:09:16.782
I think about Fred Astaire.

00:09:16.842 --> 00:09:18.744
My nan loves him.

00:09:18.804 --> 00:09:20.425
He can dance.

00:09:20.485 --> 00:09:22.576
I want to dance like him.

00:09:22.636 --> 00:09:25.178
I run and jump down the road.

00:09:25.238 --> 00:09:34.024
Fred Astaire's music is playing in my head and I feel great.

00:09:34.084 --> 00:09:46.806
Chapter 3 Billy Do the Spin I think about ballet all the time.

00:09:46.866 --> 00:09:49.667
One and two and up and down.

00:09:49.727 --> 00:09:53.568
Mrs. Words and the music are always in my head.

00:09:53.628 --> 00:09:55.578
But there's a problem.

00:09:55.638 --> 00:09:57.979
I feel stupid.

00:09:58.039 --> 00:10:00.050
And then there's my dad.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.540
And Tony.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.681
Miners don't do ballet.

00:10:03.741 --> 00:10:06.502
Miners sons don't do ballet.

00:10:06.562 --> 00:10:10.785
Miners don't do much when they're on strike.

00:10:10.845 --> 00:10:13.698
The strike is going to end soon.

00:10:13.758 --> 00:10:15.589
I heard it on the TV.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.790
The cold weather's coming.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:22.344
The strikers and their families are going to be cold and hungry.

00:10:22.404 --> 00:10:24.544
They're going to need money.

00:10:24.604 --> 00:10:28.367
The strike is going to be over by Christmas.

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:32.230
People know about the ballet at school but I don't care.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:34.310
Some of the boys laugh at me.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:37.904
Hey Billy, where are you pink ballet shoes today?

00:10:37.964 --> 00:10:39.826
What do they know?

00:10:39.887 --> 00:10:42.890
Debbie Wilkinson's always talking to me too.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.573
She and her mama posh, not like my family.

00:10:46.633 --> 00:10:49.946
She walked home with me from school the other day.

00:10:50.006 --> 00:10:53.640
Lots of boys do ballet, you know, she said.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:55.111
Don't be stupid.

00:10:55.171 --> 00:10:55.872
Who?

00:10:55.932 --> 00:10:57.624
Who do we know?

00:10:57.684 --> 00:11:00.746
No one here, but lots of men do it.

00:11:00.806 --> 00:11:02.855
Are you coming next week?

00:11:02.915 --> 00:11:04.482
She looked at me.

00:11:04.542 --> 00:11:06.083
I'm gone to boxing.

00:11:06.143 --> 00:11:07.814
My dad says, I said.

00:11:07.874 --> 00:11:09.354
I was a bit angry.

00:11:09.414 --> 00:11:10.614
Okay.

00:11:10.674 --> 00:11:12.265
She walked off.

00:11:12.325 --> 00:11:14.766
She lives in the nice part of town.

00:11:14.826 --> 00:11:17.437
In a posh house with a posh garden.

00:11:17.497 --> 00:11:20.888
Her and her mum don't know anything about our life.

00:11:20.948 --> 00:11:23.900
Then the music comes back in my head.

00:11:23.959 --> 00:11:26.070
I start to dance.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:29.510
And I forget about my life too.

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:32.561
I've got this friend, Michael.

00:11:32.621 --> 00:11:34.422
He hates football.

00:11:34.482 --> 00:11:36.134
Not like me.

00:11:36.194 --> 00:11:39.436
We're different, but we're best friends.

00:11:39.496 --> 00:11:41.728
I can talk to him about things.

00:11:41.788 --> 00:11:43.779
I told him about the ballet.

00:11:43.839 --> 00:11:45.590
I did some of the moves.

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:47.192
He thinks it's cool.

00:11:47.252 --> 00:11:49.733
Leg out, arm out, one, two, I said.

00:11:49.793 --> 00:11:50.974
Eyes to the front.

00:11:51.034 --> 00:11:52.295
Michael laughed.

00:11:52.355 --> 00:11:54.100
Oh, when's the next lesson?

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.073
I'm not going," I said.

00:11:56.133 --> 00:11:57.544
Ball is for girls.

00:11:57.604 --> 00:11:59.144
I feel stupid.

00:11:59.204 --> 00:12:01.784
You are stupid, Michael laughed.

00:12:01.844 --> 00:12:03.925
Anyway, it's not just for girls.

00:12:03.985 --> 00:12:05.145
It's different for men.

00:12:05.205 --> 00:12:06.765
Men are stronger."

00:12:06.825 --> 00:12:08.676
He was right.

00:12:08.736 --> 00:12:11.696
I can jump higher than the girls in the ballet class.

00:12:11.756 --> 00:12:14.357
And I'm better than most of them.

00:12:14.417 --> 00:12:16.547
So I went again.

00:12:16.607 --> 00:12:21.828
On Saturday, I took my 50p from the kitchen table and I went to the social.

00:12:21.888 --> 00:12:24.920
This week the class was in a different room.

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:28.092
That was good because I didn't want to see George.

00:12:28.152 --> 00:12:30.804
At the start it was boring.

00:12:30.864 --> 00:12:33.556
I didn't know the moves, so I stopped.

00:12:33.616 --> 00:12:35.328
Miss came over.

00:12:35.387 --> 00:12:37.118
What are you doing?

00:12:37.178 --> 00:12:39.630
I don't know the moves, Miss, I said.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.092
Follow the girls.

00:12:41.152 --> 00:12:43.133
Go to the back and watch them.

00:12:43.193 --> 00:12:46.166
And one, two, three.

00:12:46.226 --> 00:12:49.866
That was okay, but it was still a bit boring.

00:12:49.926 --> 00:12:52.036
Then Miss showed us the spin.

00:12:52.096 --> 00:12:55.738
You spin around and around very fast and then you stop.

00:12:55.798 --> 00:12:58.059
You must stay in the same place.

00:12:58.119 --> 00:13:00.400
It looks great, but it's very difficult.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.092
You fall on the floor a lot.

00:13:02.152 --> 00:13:03.692
We all tried it.

00:13:03.752 --> 00:13:06.113
Do it at home, Miss said.

00:13:06.174 --> 00:13:07.814
Try again and again.

00:13:07.874 --> 00:13:09.576
You can do it.

00:13:09.636 --> 00:13:13.048
At the end of the class, Miss came over to me.

00:13:13.108 --> 00:13:16.031
So, are you coming next week?

00:13:16.091 --> 00:13:17.994
I don't know, miss.

00:13:18.054 --> 00:13:20.305
She looks at my belly shoes.

00:13:20.366 --> 00:13:22.708
Give me those, then."

00:13:22.768 --> 00:13:24.638
I didn't want to.

00:13:24.698 --> 00:13:27.641
I wanted to learn the spin and do it at boxing.

00:13:27.701 --> 00:13:30.392
I wanted to see Georgie's face.

00:13:30.452 --> 00:13:34.606
No, it's okay, I said, and gave him a 50p.

00:13:34.666 --> 00:13:36.877
She took it and went off.

00:13:36.938 --> 00:13:39.249
She didn't say anything.

00:13:39.309 --> 00:13:42.740
At home, Nan was in the kitchen.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.860
Bally shoes!

00:13:44.921 --> 00:13:46.251
How lovely!"

00:13:46.311 --> 00:13:47.531
she said.

00:13:47.592 --> 00:13:50.963
Don't tell Dad, I said, and ran into my room.

00:13:51.023 --> 00:13:53.904
Luckily, Dad and Tony were out.

00:13:53.964 --> 00:13:58.115
Dad is not going to understand about Bally shoes.

00:13:58.175 --> 00:14:01.856
Dad isn't going to understand about any of this.

00:14:01.916 --> 00:14:05.528
I put the Bally shoes under my bed with my boxing things.

00:14:05.588 --> 00:14:08.539
Anyway, I'm going to go to boxing soon.

00:14:08.599 --> 00:14:16.018
I'm going to go when I can do the spin.

00:14:16.078 --> 00:14:22.178
Chapter 4.

00:14:22.238 --> 00:14:23.418
Jackie.

00:14:23.478 --> 00:14:25.580
My son Billy.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:29.603
There's something funny about Billy at the moment.

00:14:29.664 --> 00:14:32.586
He's a bit different from the other boys.

00:14:32.646 --> 00:14:33.856
I know that.

00:14:33.916 --> 00:14:36.938
But now, it's this spinning.

00:14:36.998 --> 00:14:39.110
He does it everywhere.

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:42.692
He puts out his arms and spins around and around.

00:14:42.752 --> 00:14:44.804
He looks a bit stupid.

00:14:44.864 --> 00:14:46.416
Like a girl.

00:14:46.476 --> 00:14:47.946
He doesn't care.

00:14:48.007 --> 00:14:49.528
Not Billy.

00:14:49.588 --> 00:14:52.550
It's a boxing move, he tells me.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:54.332
Boxing.

00:14:54.392 --> 00:14:57.834
Sometimes I can't believe Billy is my son.

00:14:57.894 --> 00:15:00.906
Then, there's the strike.

00:15:00.966 --> 00:15:03.708
We started four months ago.

00:15:03.768 --> 00:15:05.880
We're so poor now.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:08.532
We haven't got money for anything.

00:15:08.592 --> 00:15:10.694
What's going to happen?

00:15:10.754 --> 00:15:12.375
We don't know.

00:15:12.435 --> 00:15:15.138
Maybe they're going to close the mines.

00:15:15.198 --> 00:15:18.230
Maybe they decided a long time ago.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.870
So why are we doing this?

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.750
Tone is angry.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.331
I see it in his eyes.

00:15:24.391 --> 00:15:26.442
Every day at the mine.

00:15:26.502 --> 00:15:29.842
What's he going to do if there's no mine?

00:15:29.902 --> 00:15:32.733
Some men choose to work.

00:15:32.793 --> 00:15:35.004
We call them scabs.

00:15:35.064 --> 00:15:38.055
The strikers stand together at the mine.

00:15:38.115 --> 00:15:40.475
The scabs go through in buses.

00:15:40.535 --> 00:15:42.746
There are police everywhere.

00:15:42.806 --> 00:15:44.556
We shout at the buses.

00:15:44.616 --> 00:15:46.367
We bang on the windows.

00:15:46.427 --> 00:15:48.298
The scabs look frightened.

00:15:48.358 --> 00:15:50.268
I'm not surprised.

00:15:50.328 --> 00:15:53.209
This morning, I was next to George.

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:54.611
It was cold.

00:15:54.671 --> 00:15:56.962
We waited for the scabuses.

00:15:57.022 --> 00:15:59.455
Listen, Jackie, he said.

00:15:59.515 --> 00:16:00.846
Forget the money.

00:16:00.906 --> 00:16:02.767
The 50p for the boxing.

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:04.840
I don't do it for the money.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.500
What?

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.842
I didn't understand.

00:16:08.902 --> 00:16:10.734
It's Billy.

00:16:10.794 --> 00:16:12.986
He doesn't come to boxing now.

00:16:13.046 --> 00:16:15.118
Is it because of the money?

00:16:15.178 --> 00:16:17.440
I started to think.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.944
Where did Billy go every Saturday morning?

00:16:21.004 --> 00:16:23.877
Then a bus came in and everyone started a shout.

00:16:23.937 --> 00:16:24.537
Scab!

00:16:24.597 --> 00:16:25.028
Scab!

00:16:25.048 --> 00:16:25.288
Scab!

00:16:25.308 --> 00:16:26.679
Scab!

00:16:26.739 --> 00:16:29.231
I shouted with the other men.

00:16:29.291 --> 00:16:31.914
But I thought about other things.

00:16:31.974 --> 00:16:34.144
Tomorrow was Saturday.

00:16:34.204 --> 00:16:36.516
Billie's Boxing Day.

00:16:36.576 --> 00:16:42.982
I had an idea.

00:16:43.042 --> 00:16:49.006
Chapter 5.

00:16:49.066 --> 00:16:49.947
Billy.

00:16:50.007 --> 00:16:51.642
Just you and me.

00:16:51.702 --> 00:16:53.758
I can spin now.

00:16:53.818 --> 00:16:56.350
I can do everything, all the moves."

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:59.132
Miss teaches me for a lot of the lesson.

00:16:59.192 --> 00:17:01.865
The girls aren't happy about it.

00:17:01.925 --> 00:17:04.077
Miss, what about us?

00:17:04.137 --> 00:17:05.319
They say.

00:17:05.378 --> 00:17:06.890
She doesn't listen.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:08.451
I'm busy.

00:17:08.512 --> 00:17:10.464
Then it happened.

00:17:10.524 --> 00:17:14.247
Michael often said to me, what about your dad?

00:17:14.307 --> 00:17:15.845
What are you going to do?

00:17:15.905 --> 00:17:18.444
Yeah, it happened.

00:17:18.504 --> 00:17:20.796
I was in the centre of the class.

00:17:20.857 --> 00:17:22.839
Miss was next to me.

00:17:22.898 --> 00:17:25.252
And stretch a leg, Billy.

00:17:25.312 --> 00:17:29.326
I looked up, and there he was by the door.

00:17:29.386 --> 00:17:31.548
His face was red.

00:17:31.608 --> 00:17:33.510
Miss Oren, too.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.810
The music stopped.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.107
You!

00:17:37.167 --> 00:17:37.698
Out!

00:17:37.758 --> 00:17:38.468
Now!"

00:17:38.528 --> 00:17:39.748
he shouted.

00:17:39.808 --> 00:17:42.930
Miss wanted to say something, but I stopped her.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:44.910
I had enough problems.

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:48.502
I followed Dad out of the social.

00:17:48.562 --> 00:17:50.883
Ballet!

00:17:50.943 --> 00:17:52.554
We were in the kitchen.

00:17:52.614 --> 00:17:55.174
Dad didn't speak to me when we left the social.

00:17:55.234 --> 00:17:57.166
Maybe he was too angry.

00:17:57.226 --> 00:17:58.666
I don't know.

00:17:58.726 --> 00:18:00.537
What's wrong with Ballet?

00:18:00.597 --> 00:18:03.278
I said, lots of people do it.

00:18:03.338 --> 00:18:05.883
Dad's face was red again.

00:18:05.943 --> 00:18:08.788
Lots of girls do ballet, Billy.

00:18:08.848 --> 00:18:09.698
Not boys.

00:18:09.758 --> 00:18:12.558
Boys do football or boxing.

00:18:12.618 --> 00:18:14.489
It was true in a way.

00:18:14.549 --> 00:18:16.330
Ballet isn't boxing.

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.240
You don't hit anyone.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.320
It's not mining.

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:23.091
So my dad can't understand it.

00:18:23.151 --> 00:18:25.922
So it's not boxing or mining.

00:18:25.982 --> 00:18:27.342
Well, so what?

00:18:27.402 --> 00:18:29.123
I'm not the same as my dad.

00:18:29.183 --> 00:18:30.968
I can be different.

00:18:31.029 --> 00:18:33.304
I like dancing, Dad.

00:18:33.365 --> 00:18:34.575
That's all it is.

00:18:34.635 --> 00:18:35.525
Dancing.

00:18:35.585 --> 00:18:37.246
Why is that so bad?

00:18:37.306 --> 00:18:39.676
Listen, forget about dancing.

00:18:39.736 --> 00:18:40.767
You're not doing it.

00:18:40.827 --> 00:18:42.237
Understand?

00:18:42.297 --> 00:18:45.108
I jumped up and shouted in his face.

00:18:45.168 --> 00:18:46.428
I hate you.

00:18:46.488 --> 00:18:48.089
I run out of the house.

00:18:48.149 --> 00:18:49.479
I ran and ran.

00:18:49.539 --> 00:18:51.240
I hated my dad.

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:54.140
I loved dancing and I was good at it.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.601
I knew that.

00:18:55.661 --> 00:18:57.572
Miss knew it too.

00:18:57.632 --> 00:19:00.939
Suddenly I wanted to see her.

00:19:00.999 --> 00:19:04.038
I was in Mrs. House.

00:19:04.098 --> 00:19:05.850
It was funny.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:09.342
Me, Debbie, Miss, and her husband.

00:19:09.403 --> 00:19:11.114
He was funny, too.

00:19:11.174 --> 00:19:13.696
He was always in the pub, Debbie said.

00:19:13.756 --> 00:19:16.278
He always had a beer in his hand.

00:19:16.338 --> 00:19:18.831
Oh, it's little Jean Kelly!

00:19:18.891 --> 00:19:20.342
He said when he saw me.

00:19:20.403 --> 00:19:22.714
Be quiet, Tom, Miss said.

00:19:22.774 --> 00:19:24.816
You're not in the pub now?

00:19:24.876 --> 00:19:26.956
I had dinner with them.

00:19:27.016 --> 00:19:30.316
Later, Miss took me home in her car.

00:19:30.375 --> 00:19:33.636
She stopped near my house and looked at me.

00:19:33.696 --> 00:19:38.307
Billy, I'm thinking about the Royal Ballet School.

00:19:38.367 --> 00:19:40.927
Aren't you a bit old, Miss, I said?

00:19:40.987 --> 00:19:42.888
Not me, you.

00:19:42.948 --> 00:19:46.748
There's an audition in Newcastle in two weeks.

00:19:46.808 --> 00:19:48.689
Ballet School.

00:19:48.749 --> 00:19:50.059
Me.

00:19:50.119 --> 00:19:51.920
Ballet.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:53.860
All day.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.176
Every day.

00:19:56.236 --> 00:19:59.554
Can you do ballet as a job then, Miss?

00:19:59.614 --> 00:20:00.834
I asked her.

00:20:00.894 --> 00:20:03.886
Yes, if you're good enough.

00:20:03.946 --> 00:20:06.568
But I don't know anything.

00:20:06.628 --> 00:20:09.771
Look, she took a cigarette from her bag.

00:20:09.831 --> 00:20:11.122
They teach you.

00:20:11.182 --> 00:20:14.724
It's a school and she waited a minute.

00:20:14.784 --> 00:20:17.326
I think you're good enough.

00:20:17.386 --> 00:20:19.358
Wow.

00:20:19.418 --> 00:20:22.370
She didn't usually say anything nice.

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:24.572
What about my dad?

00:20:24.632 --> 00:20:26.968
I can speak to him if you want.

00:20:27.029 --> 00:20:29.536
No, please, Miss.

00:20:29.596 --> 00:20:31.817
I knew my dad.

00:20:31.878 --> 00:20:34.870
I can give you more lessons, she said.

00:20:34.930 --> 00:20:36.390
Just you and me.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:37.932
Don't think about the money.

00:20:37.992 --> 00:20:39.934
I'm not doing it for the money.

00:20:39.994 --> 00:20:41.624
I thought about it.

00:20:41.684 --> 00:20:44.756
My dad didn't know about it and that was wrong.

00:20:44.816 --> 00:20:47.648
But I wanted to be a dancer.

00:20:47.708 --> 00:20:49.760
I smiled at Miss.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:51.372
Okay then.

00:20:51.432 --> 00:20:53.232
She smiled too.

00:20:53.292 --> 00:20:55.788
She didn't usually smile.

00:20:55.848 --> 00:20:59.404
6 o'clock on Monday at the social, she said.

00:20:59.464 --> 00:21:02.375
Okay, I open the car door.

00:21:02.435 --> 00:21:05.647
Oh, and Billy, bring something with you.

00:21:05.707 --> 00:21:07.768
Something that's important to you.

00:21:07.827 --> 00:21:15.401
We must think of an idea for the audition dance.

00:21:15.461 --> 00:21:21.643
Chapter 6.

00:21:21.703 --> 00:21:22.924
Billy.

00:21:22.984 --> 00:21:24.852
Mam's Dance.

00:21:24.912 --> 00:21:27.341
There wasn't much time.

00:21:27.401 --> 00:21:30.142
The audition was in two weeks.

00:21:30.202 --> 00:21:32.944
I met Miss almost every night.

00:21:33.004 --> 00:21:36.415
I'm going to Michael's house, I told Dad.

00:21:36.476 --> 00:21:39.908
The first evening I had some things with me.

00:21:39.968 --> 00:21:43.519
My football, some T-Rex music.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:45.100
I liked to boogie.

00:21:45.161 --> 00:21:46.551
It was Tony's.

00:21:46.611 --> 00:21:48.132
I didn't ask him.

00:21:48.192 --> 00:21:51.374
Then there was the letter from my mum.

00:21:51.434 --> 00:21:54.278
Miss started to read the letter.

00:21:54.338 --> 00:21:57.132
Dear Billy, she stopped.

00:21:57.192 --> 00:21:59.293
Can I read this, Billy?

00:21:59.353 --> 00:22:01.294
Yeah, I said.

00:22:01.354 --> 00:22:03.765
I'm still here, Billy.

00:22:03.825 --> 00:22:06.876
You can't see me, but I am.

00:22:06.936 --> 00:22:08.487
I'm always with you.

00:22:08.547 --> 00:22:10.208
Don't forget that.

00:22:10.268 --> 00:22:11.909
And I love you.

00:22:11.969 --> 00:22:16.020
Be true to Billy Elliot, all your life.

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:19.706
Missed look to way and didn't say anything.

00:22:19.766 --> 00:22:21.540
You okay, Miss?"

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:22.680
I asked.

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:25.864
She's going to cry, I thought.

00:22:25.924 --> 00:22:30.296
She was a very special person, Billy, she said.

00:22:30.356 --> 00:22:34.300
Nah, she was just my mum, I said.

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:36.872
What did your mum like doing?

00:22:36.932 --> 00:22:38.293
She asked me.

00:22:38.353 --> 00:22:43.477
She liked music, I said, and then we listened to the T-Rex music.

00:22:43.537 --> 00:22:47.043
I liked boogie, jeered a bug boogie.

00:22:47.103 --> 00:22:51.248
I liked Boogie, on a Saturday night.

00:22:51.308 --> 00:22:54.780
It's happy music, Miss said.

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:56.630
Dance music.

00:22:56.691 --> 00:22:58.922
And your mum liked this.

00:22:58.982 --> 00:23:00.292
I?

00:23:00.352 --> 00:23:02.733
Then this is our dance, Billy.

00:23:02.793 --> 00:23:04.074
Let's go.

00:23:04.134 --> 00:23:07.225
We danced and jumped and ran around.

00:23:07.285 --> 00:23:09.566
We thought of lots of new moves.

00:23:09.626 --> 00:23:12.787
Now, think about your mum, Miss said.

00:23:12.847 --> 00:23:14.037
She's watching you.

00:23:14.097 --> 00:23:16.393
She's smiling and laughing.

00:23:16.453 --> 00:23:18.288
And it worked.

00:23:18.348 --> 00:23:21.400
I thought about ma'am and I did a great spin.

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:24.452
I was on top of the world.

00:23:24.512 --> 00:23:28.404
At home, things were very different.

00:23:28.464 --> 00:23:30.896
No one was on top of the world.

00:23:30.956 --> 00:23:34.388
There were police all over the town.

00:23:34.448 --> 00:23:36.549
They frightened me.

00:23:36.609 --> 00:23:39.070
Tony was never frightened.

00:23:39.130 --> 00:23:41.442
He shouted a lot at Dad.

00:23:41.502 --> 00:23:43.313
What's wrong with you?

00:23:43.373 --> 00:23:46.034
This strike is our only hope.

00:23:46.094 --> 00:23:48.214
Dad didn't answer.

00:23:48.274 --> 00:23:51.256
He just sat there and said nothing.

00:23:51.316 --> 00:23:54.396
I was sorry for him.

00:23:54.456 --> 00:23:59.939
Tonight, I'm in bed, and I hear something in the kitchen.

00:23:59.999 --> 00:24:02.270
It's Dad and Tony.

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:04.271
I sit up and listen.

00:24:04.331 --> 00:24:06.922
Tony sounds very angry.

00:24:06.982 --> 00:24:10.993
I'm not gonna sit at home and do nothing, he shouts.

00:24:11.053 --> 00:24:14.204
You think it's the end, but for me, it's the start.

00:24:14.264 --> 00:24:15.834
Now move.

00:24:15.894 --> 00:24:18.174
I run into the kitchen.

00:24:18.234 --> 00:24:21.376
Tony has a button, a police button.

00:24:21.436 --> 00:24:22.898
Where did he get that?

00:24:22.958 --> 00:24:24.910
What's he going to do with it?

00:24:24.970 --> 00:24:27.291
This time Dad shouts back.

00:24:27.351 --> 00:24:30.874
You're not going and you're not going to use that.

00:24:30.934 --> 00:24:32.485
He's looking at the button.

00:24:32.545 --> 00:24:34.336
Forget about the police.

00:24:34.396 --> 00:24:35.728
They're doing a job.

00:24:35.788 --> 00:24:37.298
That's all.

00:24:37.358 --> 00:24:40.441
Try and stop me then, says Tony.

00:24:40.501 --> 00:24:42.032
You can't do anything.

00:24:42.092 --> 00:24:44.544
You're nothing without ma'am.

00:24:44.604 --> 00:24:46.595
You're nothing.

00:24:46.655 --> 00:24:48.926
They're by the back door.

00:24:48.986 --> 00:24:51.388
Dad's face is white.

00:24:51.448 --> 00:24:53.858
Suddenly he hits Tony.

00:24:53.918 --> 00:24:55.350
Crack!

00:24:55.410 --> 00:24:58.001
Tony falls to the floor.

00:24:58.061 --> 00:24:59.552
Stop it!

00:24:59.612 --> 00:25:00.552
Stop it!

00:25:00.612 --> 00:25:01.964
I shout!

00:25:02.024 --> 00:25:04.645
Tony gets up slowly.

00:25:04.705 --> 00:25:06.786
He doesn't say a word.

00:25:06.846 --> 00:25:08.848
He doesn't look at Dad.

00:25:08.908 --> 00:25:11.789
He just runs out of the door.

00:25:11.849 --> 00:25:14.440
The baton is under his arm.

00:25:14.500 --> 00:25:21.770
Dad doesn't stop him this time.

00:25:21.830 --> 00:25:33.812
Chapter 7 Billy Black Friday Billy, you're not trying.

00:25:33.872 --> 00:25:35.173
Arm up.

00:25:35.234 --> 00:25:36.644
What?

00:25:36.704 --> 00:25:41.988
I'm at the social with Miss, but I can only think about last night and my dad and Tony.

00:25:42.048 --> 00:25:43.838
Eyes to the front.

00:25:43.898 --> 00:25:44.879
Bang.

00:25:44.939 --> 00:25:46.470
Dad hits Tony.

00:25:46.530 --> 00:25:48.341
Do it again, Billy.

00:25:48.401 --> 00:25:49.102
Bang.

00:25:49.162 --> 00:25:50.572
Tony's on the floor.

00:25:50.632 --> 00:25:53.028
Billy, that's not good enough.

00:25:53.088 --> 00:25:54.522
I can't.

00:25:54.582 --> 00:25:56.343
Suddenly I hate her.

00:25:56.403 --> 00:25:59.734
She's standing right next to me and smoking in my face.

00:25:59.794 --> 00:26:01.754
Do it again, she says.

00:26:01.815 --> 00:26:02.895
No.

00:26:02.955 --> 00:26:04.285
What?

00:26:04.345 --> 00:26:06.276
She can't believe it.

00:26:06.336 --> 00:26:09.367
Suddenly I am angry about everything.

00:26:09.427 --> 00:26:13.858
Last night, the audition, everything's going wrong.

00:26:13.918 --> 00:26:16.049
Tony was right about one thing.

00:26:16.109 --> 00:26:18.490
Without ma'am we're all nothing.

00:26:18.550 --> 00:26:20.948
And she's never coming back.

00:26:21.008 --> 00:26:22.996
I run out of the room.

00:26:23.056 --> 00:26:24.476
Miss follows me.

00:26:24.536 --> 00:26:27.137
Billy, I'm sorry, she says.

00:26:27.197 --> 00:26:28.808
I want to help you.

00:26:28.868 --> 00:26:30.028
No, you don't.

00:26:30.088 --> 00:26:31.389
The audition's for you.

00:26:31.449 --> 00:26:32.430
Not for me.

00:26:32.490 --> 00:26:35.310
That's not true, she says.

00:26:35.370 --> 00:26:37.092
I can't stop now.

00:26:37.152 --> 00:26:38.412
What have you got?

00:26:38.472 --> 00:26:39.372
Nothing.

00:26:39.432 --> 00:26:40.713
No dance school.

00:26:40.773 --> 00:26:41.353
What are you?

00:26:41.373 --> 00:26:42.424
You're nothing.

00:26:42.484 --> 00:26:44.544
Don't speak to me like that.

00:26:44.604 --> 00:26:46.846
Then she hits me across the face.

00:26:46.906 --> 00:26:48.896
She looks very surprised.

00:26:48.956 --> 00:26:50.772
I'm surprised too.

00:26:50.832 --> 00:26:54.960
I want to run, but I can't leave.

00:26:55.020 --> 00:26:56.982
I must dance.

00:26:57.042 --> 00:27:01.094
And because I can't leave, I start to cry.

00:27:01.154 --> 00:27:03.416
She puts out her arms.

00:27:03.476 --> 00:27:05.587
I'm sorry, Billy.

00:27:05.648 --> 00:27:09.420
And I cry in her arms for about five minutes.

00:27:09.480 --> 00:27:11.642
I can't stop.

00:27:11.702 --> 00:27:14.244
Right, she says.

00:27:14.304 --> 00:27:15.964
Is that enough?

00:27:16.024 --> 00:27:18.136
Yes, I say.

00:27:18.196 --> 00:27:19.926
Sorry, Miss.

00:27:19.986 --> 00:27:25.296
Right then, she says, let's start again.

00:27:25.356 --> 00:27:29.357
There was something different about that Friday.

00:27:29.417 --> 00:27:32.128
Black Friday, Dad called it.

00:27:32.188 --> 00:27:35.089
The audition was the next morning.

00:27:35.149 --> 00:27:38.680
I walked home after my last lesson with Miss.

00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:40.510
I was happy.

00:27:40.570 --> 00:27:43.301
I did my audition dance in my head.

00:27:43.361 --> 00:27:48.539
Then I turned into our road and saw them all.

00:27:48.599 --> 00:27:51.546
There were police everywhere.

00:27:51.606 --> 00:27:53.697
Mrs. Watts lives near us.

00:27:53.757 --> 00:27:56.008
She saw me and pulled me into her house.

00:27:56.067 --> 00:27:57.558
Get in, Billy.

00:27:57.618 --> 00:27:58.998
What's happening?

00:27:59.058 --> 00:28:00.599
It's your Tony.

00:28:00.659 --> 00:28:01.769
He's in trouble.

00:28:01.829 --> 00:28:03.329
The police wants him.

00:28:03.389 --> 00:28:04.249
Tony.

00:28:04.269 --> 00:28:07.200
I didn't understand.

00:28:07.260 --> 00:28:09.191
Where did he go at night?

00:28:09.251 --> 00:28:11.021
What did he do?

00:28:11.081 --> 00:28:16.502
My dad and Tony, especially Tony, hate the police.

00:28:16.562 --> 00:28:19.938
Now, I understand.

00:28:19.998 --> 00:28:22.154
I saw one man.

00:28:22.214 --> 00:28:24.634
He was in front of one of the police.

00:28:24.694 --> 00:28:27.836
The policeman hit him with his baton.

00:28:27.896 --> 00:28:29.546
He didn't stop.

00:28:29.606 --> 00:28:32.137
He hit him again and again.

00:28:32.197 --> 00:28:34.968
Then I saw our Tony.

00:28:35.028 --> 00:28:38.689
He ran up the road with the police all around him.

00:28:38.749 --> 00:28:40.500
They were faster than him.

00:28:40.560 --> 00:28:41.980
I ran to the door.

00:28:42.040 --> 00:28:42.860
Tony!

00:28:42.920 --> 00:28:44.121
In here!

00:28:44.181 --> 00:28:45.532
He didn't hear me.

00:28:45.592 --> 00:28:46.802
It was too loud.

00:28:46.862 --> 00:28:48.072
Everyone shouted.

00:28:48.132 --> 00:28:50.347
Batons banged on doors.

00:28:50.407 --> 00:29:02.022
After that, I saw about 20 police, all together, and our Tony was under them.

00:29:02.082 --> 00:29:11.770
Chapter 8 Tony Happy Christmas.

00:29:11.830 --> 00:29:14.954
I stared in the police station that night.

00:29:15.014 --> 00:29:17.172
There was no bed.

00:29:17.232 --> 00:29:18.949
Where do I sleep?"

00:29:19.009 --> 00:29:20.060
I asked.

00:29:20.120 --> 00:29:21.711
They laughed.

00:29:21.771 --> 00:29:23.933
I was black and blue.

00:29:23.992 --> 00:29:26.445
I hate the police.

00:29:26.505 --> 00:29:30.108
Next morning, I sat in the courtroom.

00:29:30.168 --> 00:29:33.080
There was a big policeman next to me.

00:29:33.140 --> 00:29:35.922
I saw Dad and our Billy.

00:29:35.982 --> 00:29:39.166
Dad was angry, but he didn't say anything.

00:29:39.226 --> 00:29:42.058
It was over very quickly.

00:29:42.118 --> 00:29:45.628
Pay the court 100 pounds, they said.

00:29:45.688 --> 00:29:48.988
We haven't got any money, they know that.

00:29:49.048 --> 00:29:52.880
And a happy Christmas to you too, I shouted.

00:29:52.941 --> 00:29:56.253
Get out of here, said the policeman.

00:29:56.313 --> 00:30:00.976
We walked home, me, dad and Billy.

00:30:01.037 --> 00:30:03.908
I wanted to get home and go to bed.

00:30:03.968 --> 00:30:07.020
I wanted to cry like a little boy.

00:30:07.080 --> 00:30:10.423
But there was this woman in front of our house.

00:30:10.484 --> 00:30:11.954
Who's that?

00:30:12.014 --> 00:30:13.105
I asked.

00:30:13.165 --> 00:30:14.926
She came up to Billy.

00:30:14.986 --> 00:30:16.728
Did she know him?

00:30:16.788 --> 00:30:18.650
Where were you, Billy?

00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:20.320
What happened?"

00:30:20.380 --> 00:30:24.782
Billy didn't want to say anything, but she waited.

00:30:24.842 --> 00:30:28.624
Our Tony was in court, he said quietly.

00:30:28.684 --> 00:30:30.366
I went to.

00:30:30.426 --> 00:30:32.536
He didn't look at her.

00:30:32.596 --> 00:30:36.218
Our dad looked at Billy and this woman.

00:30:36.279 --> 00:30:38.590
Did he know her too?

00:30:38.650 --> 00:30:41.613
What's going on, I thought?

00:30:41.673 --> 00:30:44.126
Let's go in, Dad said.

00:30:44.186 --> 00:30:45.656
What's all this about?"

00:30:45.716 --> 00:30:46.417
I said.

00:30:46.477 --> 00:30:47.837
I didn't want this.

00:30:47.897 --> 00:30:49.578
Things were bad enough.

00:30:49.638 --> 00:30:51.389
I didn't like this woman.

00:30:51.449 --> 00:30:52.819
She was posh.

00:30:52.879 --> 00:30:54.630
She had posh clothes.

00:30:54.690 --> 00:30:56.270
She wasn't like us.

00:30:56.330 --> 00:30:58.422
We went into the living room.

00:30:58.482 --> 00:31:00.832
Billy didn't look very happy.

00:31:00.892 --> 00:31:03.354
He's in trouble, I thought.

00:31:03.414 --> 00:31:05.704
Then she started.

00:31:05.764 --> 00:31:09.826
Today, Billy had an audition for the Royal Ballet School.

00:31:09.886 --> 00:31:14.731
I know things are difficult, but I didn't believe my ears.

00:31:14.792 --> 00:31:16.084
I laughed.

00:31:16.144 --> 00:31:18.306
I looked at Billy and laughed again.

00:31:18.366 --> 00:31:19.227
What?

00:31:19.287 --> 00:31:20.328
Ballet!"

00:31:20.388 --> 00:31:21.450
I said.

00:31:21.510 --> 00:31:24.914
I went over to the woman and shouted in her face.

00:31:24.974 --> 00:31:29.160
My brother does not do ballet, you stupid woman.

00:31:29.220 --> 00:31:32.790
My brother is not going to do ballet.

00:31:32.850 --> 00:31:35.220
Her face was white.

00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:37.952
She was frightened, but she didn't move.

00:31:38.012 --> 00:31:41.074
Don't shout at me, she said.

00:31:41.134 --> 00:31:43.477
Billy's a very good dancer.

00:31:43.537 --> 00:31:45.870
Where does he go after school every day?

00:31:45.930 --> 00:31:48.432
You don't know, and you don't care.

00:31:48.492 --> 00:31:49.983
I wanted to hit her.

00:31:50.043 --> 00:31:52.415
She knew, but she didn't care.

00:31:52.475 --> 00:31:54.948
Is Billy going to be like you?

00:31:55.008 --> 00:31:56.228
She said to me.

00:31:56.288 --> 00:31:58.300
No job, no hope.

00:31:58.360 --> 00:32:00.205
Do you want that for Billy?

00:32:00.265 --> 00:32:03.669
He's not going to be a scab, I shouted.

00:32:03.729 --> 00:32:04.629
Look at him.

00:32:04.689 --> 00:32:05.759
He's only 12.

00:32:05.819 --> 00:32:06.920
He's a child.

00:32:06.980 --> 00:32:09.890
And you're putting stupid ideas in his head.

00:32:09.950 --> 00:32:12.851
You learn better when you're young, said Billy.

00:32:12.911 --> 00:32:14.871
Shut it, I shouted at him.

00:32:14.931 --> 00:32:16.202
I turned back to her.

00:32:16.262 --> 00:32:20.883
My brother is not running around in a stupid dress for you or anyone.

00:32:20.943 --> 00:32:23.264
It's not for me, she said.

00:32:23.324 --> 00:32:24.654
It's for Billy.

00:32:24.714 --> 00:32:26.294
And then she turned to Billy.

00:32:26.354 --> 00:32:29.352
See you Billy, she said, and walked out of the house.

00:32:29.412 --> 00:32:32.150
Get out of our house, I shouted at her.

00:32:32.210 --> 00:32:33.791
And don't come back.

00:32:33.852 --> 00:32:36.383
She didn't hear her.

00:32:36.403 --> 00:32:37.924
I wanted to hit Billy then.

00:32:37.984 --> 00:32:39.816
I wanted to hit someone.

00:32:39.876 --> 00:32:42.351
But he was behind our dad.

00:32:42.411 --> 00:32:43.745
Shut up!

00:32:43.805 --> 00:32:44.776
I hate you!"

00:32:44.836 --> 00:32:45.906
he shouted at me.

00:32:45.966 --> 00:32:47.246
I looked at him.

00:32:47.306 --> 00:32:48.667
He's right.

00:32:48.727 --> 00:32:50.618
He hates me, I thought.

00:32:50.678 --> 00:32:51.868
You little!

00:32:51.928 --> 00:32:53.969
I tried to hit him, but Dad stopped me.

00:32:54.029 --> 00:32:56.580
Billy, run out of the back door.

00:32:56.640 --> 00:32:58.330
I looked at Dad.

00:32:58.390 --> 00:33:00.801
I'm gone to the pub, I said.

00:33:00.861 --> 00:33:03.062
I bang the door on my way out.

00:33:03.122 --> 00:33:10.200
And if I see that posh woman again.

00:33:10.260 --> 00:33:19.750
Chapter 9 Billy, you're in trouble now.

00:33:19.810 --> 00:33:24.183
That was the worst Christmas of my life, I said.

00:33:24.244 --> 00:33:25.744
I was with Michael.

00:33:25.804 --> 00:33:29.406
It was the day after Christmas, and we were out in the cold.

00:33:29.466 --> 00:33:34.930
No Christmas tree, no nothing, and no man.

00:33:34.990 --> 00:33:36.731
Have some of this.

00:33:36.792 --> 00:33:38.702
He had some of his dad's beer.

00:33:38.762 --> 00:33:40.344
I tried it.

00:33:40.404 --> 00:33:43.124
I don't like it, I said.

00:33:43.184 --> 00:33:44.553
What do you want to do then?

00:33:44.573 --> 00:33:45.944
That's Michael.

00:33:46.004 --> 00:33:47.856
Let's go to the social.

00:33:47.916 --> 00:33:51.440
Why, Michael asked, there's no one there now.

00:33:51.500 --> 00:33:55.534
So let's go, I said, and we went.

00:33:55.594 --> 00:33:59.108
Michael and I were in the boxing club.

00:33:59.168 --> 00:34:03.124
Okay, I said, you're the girl.

00:34:03.184 --> 00:34:05.938
Up and one and two.

00:34:05.998 --> 00:34:07.989
We did some of the moves together.

00:34:08.049 --> 00:34:09.639
It was good to dance again.

00:34:09.699 --> 00:34:11.540
Suddenly Michael stopped.

00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:12.820
What is it?

00:34:12.881 --> 00:34:14.571
I looked at the door.

00:34:14.631 --> 00:34:16.622
It was my dad.

00:34:16.682 --> 00:34:19.293
This time I didn't want to run.

00:34:19.353 --> 00:34:21.224
I didn't care.

00:34:21.284 --> 00:34:23.554
I walked over to him.

00:34:23.615 --> 00:34:25.365
I looked at him.

00:34:25.425 --> 00:34:28.356
And then I did my audition dance.

00:34:28.417 --> 00:34:30.667
I jumped and spun.

00:34:30.727 --> 00:34:33.493
I wanted to show dad everything.

00:34:33.553 --> 00:34:37.139
When I finished, he didn't say anything.

00:34:37.199 --> 00:34:40.460
He looked at me and ran out of the room.

00:34:40.520 --> 00:34:43.801
Billy, what did you do that for?

00:34:43.861 --> 00:34:45.001
said Michael.

00:34:45.062 --> 00:34:47.792
You're in big trouble now.

00:34:47.852 --> 00:34:52.934
He was right, but, well, that was Billy Elliot.

00:34:52.994 --> 00:34:55.265
Billy Elliot dances.

00:34:55.325 --> 00:35:01.394
That was me.

00:35:01.455 --> 00:35:07.384
Chapter 10.

00:35:07.444 --> 00:35:08.626
Jackie.

00:35:08.686 --> 00:35:10.708
The Scab Bus.

00:35:10.768 --> 00:35:13.720
I'm almost running down that road.

00:35:13.780 --> 00:35:15.030
Billy.

00:35:15.090 --> 00:35:16.922
Our Billy.

00:35:16.982 --> 00:35:18.914
He's good at something.

00:35:18.974 --> 00:35:19.644
No.

00:35:19.704 --> 00:35:20.615
Not good.

00:35:20.675 --> 00:35:22.336
Fantastic.

00:35:22.396 --> 00:35:25.178
Now, I don't know much about Bally.

00:35:25.238 --> 00:35:29.621
It's for posh people like that Mrs. Wilkinson, but maybe.

00:35:29.682 --> 00:35:31.859
Just maybe.

00:35:31.919 --> 00:35:37.146
My head spinning, and I'm thinking about my Sarah, my wife.

00:35:37.206 --> 00:35:39.357
I can almost hear her.

00:35:39.417 --> 00:35:41.417
Help the boy, Jackie.

00:35:41.477 --> 00:35:42.808
What's wrong with you?

00:35:42.868 --> 00:35:44.718
He's our son.

00:35:44.778 --> 00:35:46.629
She's right.

00:35:46.689 --> 00:35:49.429
That Mrs. Wilkinson is right, too.

00:35:49.490 --> 00:35:51.060
I'm gonna see her.

00:35:51.120 --> 00:35:53.030
Now.

00:35:53.091 --> 00:35:56.181
Her husband opens the door.

00:35:56.241 --> 00:35:57.942
He looks at me.

00:35:58.002 --> 00:36:00.165
In there, he says.

00:36:00.225 --> 00:36:02.269
I go into the living room.

00:36:02.329 --> 00:36:04.821
There she is with her cigarettes.

00:36:04.881 --> 00:36:06.952
How much has it gone to cost?

00:36:07.012 --> 00:36:08.034
I ask her.

00:36:08.094 --> 00:36:12.196
Happy Christmas to you too, she says, then she smiles.

00:36:12.256 --> 00:36:13.858
Sit down.

00:36:13.918 --> 00:36:15.239
I'm okay.

00:36:15.299 --> 00:36:17.030
I don't want to stay for long.

00:36:17.091 --> 00:36:18.362
How much?

00:36:18.422 --> 00:36:24.356
For the audition, the cost of the bus to London and a hotel for the night.

00:36:24.416 --> 00:36:26.390
I can help.

00:36:26.450 --> 00:36:29.595
I don't want your money, I say.

00:36:29.655 --> 00:36:31.795
How good is he?

00:36:31.856 --> 00:36:34.866
She smokes her cigarette and looks at me.

00:36:34.926 --> 00:36:37.998
He's the best, Mr. Elliot.

00:36:38.058 --> 00:36:39.538
Thanks.

00:36:39.598 --> 00:36:41.018
I leave.

00:36:41.078 --> 00:36:42.859
I need time.

00:36:42.919 --> 00:36:44.520
I must think.

00:36:44.580 --> 00:36:46.650
What can I do?

00:36:46.710 --> 00:36:50.432
But I already know the answer.

00:36:50.492 --> 00:36:55.610
It's six o'clock in the morning, and I'm waiting for the boss with the other men.

00:36:55.670 --> 00:36:58.210
It's the scab bus.

00:36:58.270 --> 00:37:00.441
I'm doing it for Billy.

00:37:00.501 --> 00:37:02.072
I must help him.

00:37:02.132 --> 00:37:03.864
He's my son.

00:37:03.924 --> 00:37:06.476
I didn't sleep last night.

00:37:06.536 --> 00:37:08.736
I'm doing it for one week.

00:37:08.796 --> 00:37:11.939
One week's money for our Billy's audition.

00:37:11.999 --> 00:37:14.050
Our Tony doesn't know.

00:37:14.110 --> 00:37:15.942
No one knows yet.

00:37:16.002 --> 00:37:18.310
Only the other scabs.

00:37:18.370 --> 00:37:21.480
The bus comes and we all get on.

00:37:21.540 --> 00:37:24.332
No one speaks as we drive there.

00:37:24.392 --> 00:37:27.446
When we arrive, I can hear the men.

00:37:27.506 --> 00:37:30.909
Scab, scab, scab, they shout.

00:37:30.970 --> 00:37:32.792
I know the words.

00:37:32.852 --> 00:37:35.044
I shouted them last week.

00:37:35.104 --> 00:37:37.266
We drive through the men.

00:37:37.326 --> 00:37:41.238
Bang, bang, bang, they bang on the bus windows.

00:37:41.298 --> 00:37:43.536
The police try to stop them.

00:37:43.596 --> 00:37:45.397
The bus stops.

00:37:45.457 --> 00:37:48.067
Their faces are so close.

00:37:48.127 --> 00:37:50.158
I'm very frightened now.

00:37:50.218 --> 00:37:52.048
I look around me.

00:37:52.108 --> 00:37:55.369
Some of the scabs put their hands over their faces.

00:37:55.429 --> 00:37:56.569
Not me.

00:37:56.629 --> 00:37:58.320
I don't care.

00:37:58.380 --> 00:38:01.930
I look out of the window and then I see him.

00:38:01.990 --> 00:38:04.000
It's Tony.

00:38:04.060 --> 00:38:06.301
He's looking back at me.

00:38:06.361 --> 00:38:08.802
He can't believe his eyes.

00:38:08.862 --> 00:38:11.184
I don't know what to do.

00:38:11.244 --> 00:38:15.148
He can't believe his eyes.

00:38:15.208 --> 00:38:18.490
The bus moves on.

00:38:18.550 --> 00:38:20.800
Dad!

00:38:20.860 --> 00:38:22.021
Dad!

00:38:22.081 --> 00:38:23.562
What are you doing?

00:38:23.622 --> 00:38:25.112
I'm off the bus.

00:38:25.172 --> 00:38:27.604
I'm going to go into the mine.

00:38:27.664 --> 00:38:29.464
And there he is.

00:38:29.524 --> 00:38:31.135
Our Tony.

00:38:31.195 --> 00:38:33.056
He's calling to me.

00:38:33.116 --> 00:38:35.416
He's like a little boy again.

00:38:35.476 --> 00:38:37.623
I go over to him.

00:38:37.684 --> 00:38:39.911
I'm sorry, son.

00:38:39.971 --> 00:38:42.693
It's for Billy, I say.

00:38:42.753 --> 00:38:44.694
And then I start to cry.

00:38:44.754 --> 00:38:47.196
You can't go back, Dad.

00:38:47.256 --> 00:38:48.916
Not now.

00:38:48.976 --> 00:38:53.159
Tony looks at me, and he's crying too.

00:38:53.220 --> 00:38:55.841
There's another way, Dad.

00:38:55.901 --> 00:38:57.742
We can help Billy.

00:38:57.803 --> 00:39:00.066
Please.

00:39:00.127 --> 00:39:03.391
So I didn't go into the mine.

00:39:03.451 --> 00:39:05.532
I went home without Tony.

00:39:05.592 --> 00:39:08.244
I told him all about Billy in the ballet.

00:39:08.304 --> 00:39:11.196
We're gonna find that money, Dad," he said.

00:39:11.256 --> 00:39:13.527
Billy's going to the audition.

00:39:13.587 --> 00:39:16.048
Tony had to be strong.

00:39:16.108 --> 00:39:17.690
I wasn't.

00:39:17.750 --> 00:39:23.626
Not now.

00:39:23.686 --> 00:39:29.682
Chapter 11.

00:39:29.742 --> 00:39:30.813
Billy.

00:39:30.873 --> 00:39:33.163
A stupid dream.

00:39:33.224 --> 00:39:36.644
I'm on a bus to London with me, Dad.

00:39:36.705 --> 00:39:38.865
I can't believe it.

00:39:38.925 --> 00:39:41.746
Wasn't it all a stupid dream?

00:39:41.806 --> 00:39:45.007
Me and the Royal Ballet School.

00:39:45.067 --> 00:39:48.248
But people in the town helped with the money.

00:39:48.308 --> 00:39:50.549
We had a dance at the social.

00:39:50.609 --> 00:39:54.320
And then, there were some of my mom's things.

00:39:54.380 --> 00:39:58.303
I'm going to seldom, Dad said one morning.

00:39:58.363 --> 00:40:01.206
I don't want to think about that."

00:40:01.266 --> 00:40:05.658
I hated the Royal Ballet School when I saw it.

00:40:05.718 --> 00:40:08.399
It was so big and posh.

00:40:08.459 --> 00:40:11.680
How much is this going to cost, Dad said?

00:40:11.740 --> 00:40:14.062
I changed into my dance clothes.

00:40:14.122 --> 00:40:15.802
There were other boys there.

00:40:15.862 --> 00:40:17.553
They were posh too.

00:40:17.613 --> 00:40:20.184
They didn't understand my English.

00:40:20.245 --> 00:40:21.405
Sorry?

00:40:21.465 --> 00:40:22.425
What did you say?

00:40:22.445 --> 00:40:24.404
Oh, shut it.

00:40:24.464 --> 00:40:26.934
Then there was the audition.

00:40:26.994 --> 00:40:30.476
There were five people from the Royal Ballet School there.

00:40:30.536 --> 00:40:32.748
They sat behind a long table.

00:40:32.808 --> 00:40:34.470
They didn't like me.

00:40:34.530 --> 00:40:37.142
Do you have some music, Billy?

00:40:37.203 --> 00:40:38.874
I gave it to them.

00:40:38.934 --> 00:40:40.545
T-Rex.

00:40:40.606 --> 00:40:42.557
It wasn't right for that place.

00:40:42.617 --> 00:40:44.218
I know that now.

00:40:44.278 --> 00:40:46.110
I didn't dance.

00:40:46.170 --> 00:40:47.752
I didn't move.

00:40:47.812 --> 00:40:49.954
I just looked at them.

00:40:50.014 --> 00:40:53.314
Then I heard Miss in my ear.

00:40:53.375 --> 00:40:55.984
Billy, you're not trying.

00:40:56.044 --> 00:40:57.124
Go on.

00:40:57.184 --> 00:40:58.806
Just do it."

00:40:58.866 --> 00:41:00.896
So I did it.

00:41:00.956 --> 00:41:02.737
Badly.

00:41:02.797 --> 00:41:06.268
When I finished, nobody said anything.

00:41:06.328 --> 00:41:08.540
They wrote some things down.

00:41:08.600 --> 00:41:12.311
Then one of them said, thank you Billy.

00:41:12.371 --> 00:41:14.102
You can go now.

00:41:14.162 --> 00:41:16.653
I almost ran out of there.

00:41:16.713 --> 00:41:18.124
All that work.

00:41:18.184 --> 00:41:19.334
All that money.

00:41:19.395 --> 00:41:20.745
For nothing.

00:41:20.805 --> 00:41:23.934
I just wanted to go home.

00:41:23.995 --> 00:41:26.804
But it wasn't over.

00:41:26.864 --> 00:41:30.036
They called me and Dad into the audition room again.

00:41:30.096 --> 00:41:32.928
We sat in front of that long table.

00:41:32.988 --> 00:41:37.500
Now, Billy, we have some questions for you, one of them said.

00:41:37.560 --> 00:41:39.642
Why do you like ballet?

00:41:39.702 --> 00:41:41.472
I didn't answer.

00:41:41.533 --> 00:41:43.444
I wasn't right for this place.

00:41:43.504 --> 00:41:45.094
Don't know, I said.

00:41:45.154 --> 00:41:47.926
Well, what do you like about dancing?

00:41:47.986 --> 00:41:50.698
Dad looked at me.

00:41:50.758 --> 00:41:53.230
Everything.

00:41:53.290 --> 00:41:56.462
He dances all the time, my dad said.

00:41:56.522 --> 00:42:03.364
Yes, we've got a letter from Mrs Wilkinson here, and you, Mr. Elliot, do you like ballet?

00:42:03.424 --> 00:42:06.925
Well, I don't know much about it, Dad said.

00:42:06.985 --> 00:42:10.496
Well, that was true, and that was about it.

00:42:10.556 --> 00:42:13.286
We got up and walked to the door.

00:42:13.346 --> 00:42:17.798
One more thing, Billy, said a very posh woman.

00:42:17.858 --> 00:42:21.638
How do you feel when you dance?

00:42:21.698 --> 00:42:23.844
I thought for a minute.

00:42:23.904 --> 00:42:27.442
I feel good, I started.

00:42:27.502 --> 00:42:34.936
When I dance, I forget the world and the strike and everything.

00:42:34.996 --> 00:42:37.648
There's fire in my body.

00:42:37.708 --> 00:42:42.522
It's like, it's like flying.

00:42:42.582 --> 00:42:50.278
That sounded stupid, I thought.

00:42:50.338 --> 00:42:56.314
Chapter 12.

00:42:56.374 --> 00:42:57.485
Jackie.

00:42:57.545 --> 00:42:59.305
The letter.

00:42:59.365 --> 00:43:01.436
Poor Billy.

00:43:01.496 --> 00:43:04.256
When we got home, he went to bed.

00:43:04.316 --> 00:43:06.327
He didn't want any dinner.

00:43:06.387 --> 00:43:08.558
He didn't want to talk.

00:43:08.618 --> 00:43:11.078
And that place.

00:43:11.138 --> 00:43:13.629
It was a different world.

00:43:13.689 --> 00:43:15.920
All those rich boys.

00:43:15.980 --> 00:43:18.000
Special dancing lessons.

00:43:18.060 --> 00:43:19.231
Big houses.

00:43:19.291 --> 00:43:20.641
Posh cars.

00:43:20.701 --> 00:43:23.159
It wasn't us.

00:43:23.219 --> 00:43:26.708
The Royal Ballet people.

00:43:26.768 --> 00:43:29.420
Maybe they weren't so bad.

00:43:29.480 --> 00:43:37.223
When we left the audition room, one of the teachers said, Good luck with the strike, Mr. Elliot.

00:43:37.284 --> 00:43:40.275
We waited one week.

00:43:40.336 --> 00:43:42.086
Two weeks.

00:43:42.147 --> 00:43:44.728
Then the letter arrived.

00:43:44.788 --> 00:43:46.559
Billy was at school.

00:43:46.619 --> 00:43:48.409
It was a long day.

00:43:48.470 --> 00:43:51.081
Billy came home at four o'clock.

00:43:51.141 --> 00:43:53.488
We were all there.

00:43:53.549 --> 00:43:56.275
Billy took the letter.

00:43:56.336 --> 00:43:58.806
No one said anything.

00:43:58.866 --> 00:44:02.927
He went into his nan's room and closed the door.

00:44:02.987 --> 00:44:06.558
Then, nothing.

00:44:06.618 --> 00:44:08.958
He didn't come out.

00:44:09.018 --> 00:44:12.080
In the end we went in there.

00:44:12.140 --> 00:44:14.190
I opened the door.

00:44:14.250 --> 00:44:17.300
Billy started to cry.

00:44:17.360 --> 00:44:21.212
I did it, he said quietly.

00:44:21.272 --> 00:44:23.826
I'm in.

00:44:23.886 --> 00:44:27.262
Yes!

00:44:27.282 --> 00:44:29.302
I ran up the road to the social.

00:44:29.362 --> 00:44:30.493
He did it.

00:44:30.553 --> 00:44:31.674
Our Billy.

00:44:31.734 --> 00:44:33.864
I wanted to tell everyone.

00:44:33.924 --> 00:44:35.765
I ran into the social.

00:44:35.825 --> 00:44:36.866
He's in.

00:44:36.926 --> 00:44:38.216
He did it.

00:44:38.276 --> 00:44:40.107
Nobody answered.

00:44:40.167 --> 00:44:42.348
It's over, Jackie.

00:44:42.408 --> 00:44:44.278
We're going back.

00:44:44.339 --> 00:44:45.800
What?

00:44:45.860 --> 00:44:48.020
The strike's over.

00:44:48.080 --> 00:44:51.486
We're going back to work on Monday.

00:44:51.546 --> 00:44:54.072
So that was it.

00:44:54.132 --> 00:44:57.635
The mind didn't stay open very long after that.

00:44:57.695 --> 00:45:00.276
That was ten years ago now.

00:45:00.336 --> 00:45:02.748
It was the end for me.

00:45:02.808 --> 00:45:06.400
But life is only just starting for Billy.

00:45:06.460 --> 00:45:12.884
And that's something.

00:45:12.944 --> 00:45:18.697
Epilogue.

00:45:18.758 --> 00:45:19.958
Jackie.

00:45:20.018 --> 00:45:21.788
Our Billy.

00:45:21.848 --> 00:45:24.688
Well, London doesn't change.

00:45:24.748 --> 00:45:26.460
It's still big.

00:45:26.520 --> 00:45:31.234
It's still expensive, but we didn't pay for our ballet tickets.

00:45:31.294 --> 00:45:33.756
I'm sitting here without Oni.

00:45:33.817 --> 00:45:36.780
It's funny to see your name in big letters.

00:45:36.840 --> 00:45:38.020
There.

00:45:38.080 --> 00:45:41.024
On the front of the Royal Opera House.

00:45:41.084 --> 00:45:43.154
The Royal Ballet.

00:45:43.214 --> 00:45:45.246
Billy Elliot.

00:45:45.306 --> 00:45:47.368
Our Billy.

00:45:47.428 --> 00:45:50.058
Then the music starts.

00:45:50.118 --> 00:45:51.888
And there he is.

00:45:51.948 --> 00:45:54.830
He runs on and jumps.

00:45:54.890 --> 00:45:56.200
What a jump.

00:45:56.260 --> 00:45:58.281
No one does it like Billy.

00:45:58.341 --> 00:46:00.472
He spins and spins.

00:46:00.532 --> 00:46:01.732
Everyone's watching.

00:46:01.792 --> 00:46:03.392
He's the best.

00:46:03.453 --> 00:46:05.543
And he's smiling all the time.

00:46:05.563 --> 00:46:07.054
He's smiling at us.

00:46:07.114 --> 00:46:11.236
So I stand up and I shout, Billy, Billy Elliot.

00:46:11.296 --> 00:46:13.126
Tone is standing with me.

00:46:13.186 --> 00:46:15.227
Our Billy, he shouts.

00:46:15.287 --> 00:46:17.613
And other people stand up too.

00:46:17.673 --> 00:46:21.114
And you know, I'm never gonna forget this.

00:46:21.174 --> 00:46:24.010
It's the best time of my life.

